// Requires Concerto 4: this model uses a map type, which concerto-core 3.x
// only accepts behind the enableMapType flag that the models build does not set.
concerto version "^4.0.0"

namespace org.accordproject.runtime@1.0.0

import org.accordproject.agreement@1.0.0.Agreement from https://models.accordproject.org/accordproject/agreement@1.0.0.cto
import org.accordproject.crypto@1.0.0.ContentHash from https://models.accordproject.org/crypto/crypto@1.0.0.cto

/**
 * Base request for invoking contract logic with no custom request properties.
 */
transaction Request {
}

/**
 * Base response for contract logic with no custom response properties.
 */
transaction Response {
}

/**
 * The extension point for template-specific runtime state.
 *
 * A template declares one concrete subtype and it is carried in
 * AgreementState.data, or in ClauseState.data for state scoped to a clause.
 * This mirrors agreement@1.0.0.TemplateData: state is composed into the
 * envelope rather than subclassing it.
 */
abstract concept StateData {}

/**
 * The state of a single clause instance.
 *
 * This concept holds nothing but the clause's state data, and exists only to
 * carry it. The map below would otherwise take StateData directly, which is
 * what it means; the indirection is a workaround, not a modelling decision.
 *
 * Reason: a map value whose concrete type is imported from another namespace
 * cannot be (de)serialized, and a template's StateData subtype always is. See
 * accordproject/concerto#1279, which is open and unreleased as of 4.1.5.
 * Declaring the value as a concept and putting the polymorphic property in a
 * field avoids the affected code path. Once that fix ships and this repository
 * moves off a pinned concerto-core, collapse this concept into the map.
 *
 * There is deliberately no lifecycle status property, and no repeat of the
 * clause path: the path is the map key. What it means for a clause to be, for
 * example, active or breached is a matter for the template and its logic, not
 * for this model, so the status vocabulary belongs in the concrete StateData
 * subtype a template declares.
 */
concept ClauseState {
  o StateData data
}

/**
 * The state of an agreement's clause instances, keyed by clause instance path.
 *
 * Keys are the instance paths defined by agreement@1.0.0.Clause.path, for
 * example "payment" or "deliveries[2].inspection", and mirror the keys of the
 * corresponding AgreementDocument.clauses map.
 */
map ClauseStates {
  o String
  o ClauseState
}

/**
 * An identified, revisioned snapshot of the whole runtime state of an
 * agreement, including the state of each of its clause instances.
 *
 * State is held as one document per agreement rather than one asset per
 * clause. A transition which spans scopes, such as marking a clause BREACHED
 * because of a condition detected in the agreement or in a peer clause, is
 * then a single write producing a single revision and a single hash, and
 * sibling state is in scope without a further lookup. Per-clause state assets
 * would require a cross-asset transaction that Concerto does not provide, and
 * would leave revision and previousStateHash without a well-defined meaning.
 *
 * The keys of clauseStates mirror the keys of the corresponding
 * AgreementDocument.clauses maps, so the state tree has the same shape as the
 * clause structure and can be navigated with ordinary property access in a
 * host language. Scoping rules for that navigation are deliberately not
 * encoded in the model.
 *
 * stateHash commits to the canonical state representation, excluding the
 * stateHash property itself. previousStateHash links a revision to its
 * immediate predecessor when one exists.
 *
 * Obligations are intentionally not defined in this namespace. New
 * implementations should use org.accordproject.obligation@1.0.0 so durable
 * obligation state and lifecycle events are not coupled to the runtime API.
 */
asset AgreementState identified by stateId {
  o String stateId
  --> Agreement agreement
  o Long revision default=0 range=[0,]
  o DateTime effectiveAt
  o StateData data optional
  o ClauseStates clauseStates optional
  o ContentHash stateHash
  o ContentHash previousStateHash optional
}
